From: Dmitry R <rdmitry0911@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH 0/1] RFC WebRTC console API for graphical LXC consoles
To: pve-devel@lists.proxmox.com
Cc: Alexandre Derumier <alexandre.derumier@groupe-cyllene.com>

Base: pve-container c8132559faedb76a56498d411bf3e024c1ff07e7 (6.1.13).
Apply shared-guest-common before webrtc-qemu-server0002 or webrtc-pve-container.

The API authorizes VM.Console for offers/status/settings reads and
VM.Config.Options for settings writes. Protected, node-proxied methods
send guest kind/VMID and the authorized user to a root-owned local Unix
socket. Media remains with a separately packaged console service. No
browser ticket, display FD or browser-selected filesystem path is passed.

Both native VM and LXC signalling use the existing PVE HTTPS origin8006;
only WebRTC media needs its negotiated UDP transport. The stock LXC
terminal console remains available. LXC graphic session provisioning,
slot isolation and encoding remain in the console provider, not PVE.

Local package version suffixes identify the tested review build. See
review-native-lxc-2026-10-15 for package hashes and runtime evidence.
